CampusOps — Phase 4.5 verification log
Scope correction (access QRs, complaints, club faculty) + hardening
Run on 2026-11-01, Bun 1.4.4, PostgreSQL 17.11, sandbox Linux.

Every gate below was run AFTER the last code change. Commands are the ones the
user can re-run after exporting the repo and filling in .env.

=== 1. Lint ===
$ bun run lint
Checked 151 files. No fixes applied. 0 errors.

=== 2. Typecheck (all three workspaces) ===
$ bun run typecheck
@campusops/shared typecheck: Exited with code 0
@campusops/api    typecheck: Exited with code 0
@campusops/web    typecheck: Exited with code 0

=== 3. Database ===
$ bun run db:migrate      # campusops_dev and campusops_test
0001_init.sql .. 0006_access_qr_and_club_faculty.sql applied; migrations complete.
$ bun run db:seed         # both databases
seed complete (idempotent)   — run twice, no duplicates
$ bun run db:check
Exited with code 0

Migration 0006 was amended twice during this round (scan_logs.event_id, and
dropping the legacy one-redemption-per-checkpoint constraint). Both databases
were therefore recreated from scratch and migrated 0001→0006 so that the files
and the live schema are identical. No migration was edited after being applied
to a database that was kept.

=== 4. Tests ===
$ bun run test
224 pass / 0 fail / 1787 expect() calls / 18 files.

New files this round (only the corrected code is tested, per instruction):
  tests/access-rules.test.ts          20 tests — pure access rules + QR codec
  tests/access.integration.test.ts    34 tests — HTTP + real DB
  tests/complaints.integration.test.ts 21 tests — HTTP + real DB + PDF bytes

Previously-passing suites were NOT rewritten. Four existing assertions were
updated because the approved scope change made them obsolete:
  - demo user count 11 → 10 (the separate scanning-staff account was removed)
    in constraints.integration.test.ts and db.integration.test.ts
  - HOD/Dean may now manage clubs in their own department
    (phase2.integration.test.ts: 403 → 200, plus a NEW 403 assertion for a club
     in another department, so the test is stronger than before)
  - "the faculty advisor may search too" → "club faculty help run events but do
    not manage the club team" (phase4.integration.test.ts: 200 → 403)
Two constraint tests stopped asserting on driver message text and now assert
the PostgreSQL condition code, which survives driver/ORM upgrades.

