=== 8. Dependency audit ===
$ bun audit   (before)
6 vulnerabilities: 3 high, 2 moderate, 1 low
$ bun audit   (after)
4 vulnerabilities: 1 high, 2 moderate, 1 low

Fixed:
  drizzle-orm 0.38.4 → 0.45.4   HIGH CVE-2026-39356 (SQL identifier injection)
  playwright  1.49.1 → 1.64.1   HIGH GHSA-7mvr-c777-76hp (browser download TLS)
Also updated within range: hono 4.13.16, @aws-sdk/* 3.1161.0,
zod-to-json-schema 3.25.2. All gates re-run after the upgrades.

Remaining, with reasoning in phase4.5-audit.md:
  zod 3.25.76 (high, CVE-2023-54404) — patched only in Zod 4.6.6. The actual
    vector (unbounded array schemas) has been closed in our code; see audit.
  deepmerge / glob / minimatch — transitive under apps/mobile > expo. They are
    build-time tooling for the mobile app, which is the next phase.

=== 9. Not exercised, and not claimed ===
- S3 and Brevo with real credentials. STORAGE_MODE and EMAIL_MODE still run in
  demo mode here; the user supplies real values.
- Render / Vercel / Neon deployment itself.
- A physical QR scan from a phone camera. The QR payload is verified
  module-by-module against the encoder in a test, and the scan API is verified
  end-to-end over HTTP, but no camera has read a printed poster yet.
